# CORE #11/#12 REGRESSION — `&hm["k"]` write-through on
# `HashMap[String, int]` (call-arg amp face).
#
# AXIS PIN: HashMap[String, int] · scalar-value · `&hm[k]` call-arg
# amp · elem-type `HashMap__GorgetString__int64_t` → resolved via
# `infer_collection_element_type` (methods.rs). Kind-gate at
# `try_resolve_index_element_ptr` must ADMIT `CollectionKind::Map`.
#
# RED-VERIFIED PRE-FIX (Round XXIII δ scout 2026-08-01): printed
# `10` on BOTH backends (should be `11`). Two blockers:
#   (a) `infer_collection_element_type` no `HashMap__` arm → falls
#       to `I64_TYPE`.
#   (b) `try_resolve_index_element_ptr` kind-gate admitted only
#       `Array | OrderedMap` → HashMap (kind `Map`) returned `None`
#       before any lowering, falling through to a value-copy
#       `hm[k]`, so the callee's `&` write hit a throwaway.
#
# INTENDED post-fix: `11`, matching the Dict/Vector controls.
#
# Rehash-invalidation aliasing shares Vector's realloc invariant —
# the D10(b) syntactic call-arg overlap check trips uniformly on
# `f(&hm[k], &hm[k])` (verified live 2026-08-01, `E_BorrowConflict`);
# the deeper D10 structural chokepoint (TODO.md:121 High) is owed.
from std.collections import HashMap

void bump(int &n):
    n = n + 1

void main():
    HashMap[String, int] hm = HashMap[String, int]()
    hm["k"] = 10
    bump(&hm["k"])
    print(hm["k"])
